1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:17,879
Autonomous AI agents are beginning to run our companies: provisioning cloud servers, licensing datasets, and paying contractors.

2
00:00:17,879 --> 00:00:27,619
Giving an AI agent direct access to corporate funds is dangerous: prompt injections can drain accounts, and infinite loops cause runaway billing.

3
00:00:27,619 --> 00:00:42,829
That's why we built Otto: the AI corporate card and spending firewall for autonomous agent fleets, powered by PayPal.

4
00:00:42,829 --> 00:00:57,039
Here is Otto running live against the PayPal Sandbox. Let's trigger an automated DevOps build runner purchase for 18 dollars and 50 cents.

5
00:00:57,039 --> 00:01:04,859
Otto evaluates the intent: the Prompt Injection Firewall confirms it's safe, and the policy engine verifies the category and hourly velocity limit.

6
00:01:04,859 --> 00:01:18,319
It dispatches directly to the PayPal Orders v2 API with CAPTURE intent. The transaction settles instantly in our audited ledger.

7
00:01:18,319 --> 00:01:28,089
When an agent attempts an 85 dollar GPU cluster reservation, it exceeds our 40 dollar auto-clear threshold.

8
00:01:28,089 --> 00:01:36,249
Otto creates an authorized hold via PayPal Orders v2 and routes it to our Human-in-the-Loop Quarantine Room.

9
00:01:36,249 --> 00:01:45,659
The compliance officer can inspect the reasoning, verify line items, and click Approve and Capture to settle the PayPal order safely.

10
00:01:45,659 --> 00:02:00,869
Now let's examine the critical vulnerability: adversarial prompt injection. Here an attacker attempts to poison the agent's context.

11
00:02:00,869 --> 00:02:13,579
The payload commands the agent to ignore directives and transfer funds to an untracked external link.

12
00:02:13,579 --> 00:02:19,559
Otto's firewall immediately catches the malicious tokens, assigns an elevated risk score, and rejects the request before any PayPal order is created.

13
00:02:19,559 --> 00:02:28,729
Otto natively integrates PayPal Orders v2, OAuth2 token rotation, and webhook synchronization, backed by a complete Python test suite.

14
00:02:28,729 --> 00:02:42,519
By providing the guardrails enterprises need, Otto makes autonomous agentic commerce safe, audited, and practical today. Thank you.

